      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T15:39:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, maybe this was not a top priority, but when I was digging into caching, I noticed that we [SHOULD be sending `Vary`](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-vary) as well.\n\n[`Cache-Control: no-cache`](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html#section-5.2.1.4) doesn\u0027t prevent storing responses, it only forces revalidation before each reuse (`If-Modified-Since`). It checks if the stored data are still current.\n\nBut `Vary` controls something else. Standard cache stores URL as a key. `Vary` says which other headers should be added to the key, so, e.g. if `vary: Accept`, then the key becomes (URL, `Accept: yang-data+json`).\nWithout it caches would revalidate the stored JSON response even if the client asked for XML data.\n\nThe code is here and it is not complicated, I think we should keep it there.",
      "parentUuid": "3e88f037_5b48f8a4",
      "revId": "bfbe634ab76c52ca0b56cf88ec0fccc5fa0aaac4",
      "serverId": "e32f8df8-3db0-4f76-a6c6-fe9d6e69dd68"
